  "title": "Unfriendly partitions",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "If $G$ is a graph, we say that a partition of $V(G)$ is unfriendly if every vertex has at least as many neighbors in the other classes as in its own.\n\nProblem Does every countably infinite graph have an unfriendly partition into two sets?",
